{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"world-sensors","name":"Soil, water, gas, flame, magnet and pulse sensors","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Sensors for the world around a project: soil moisture (capacitive), water level, MQ-2 gas and smoke (with its warm-up), an IR flame sensor, a hall-effect magnet sensor and a pulse (heartbeat) sensor. What they sense is set in the run panel while it runs: how wet the soil is, how much gas, a finger on the pulse sensor.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// Sensors of the world around a project. What they sense comes from the run panel's controls; what\n// they put out is what the real modules do (their output voltages, their comparators, warm-up).\n\nconst clamp = (x, a, b) => Math.max(a, Math.min(b, x));\n/** a little noise, as on every real analog sensor (a few mV) */\nconst noise = (v) => v * (1 + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.004);\n\nbench.device('soil', (part) => {\n  const wet = part.control('wet');\n  let out = 0, vcc = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      vcc = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      if (vcc < 3) { io.release('AOUT'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      // (capacitive v1.2: ~2.4 V in dry soil, ~1.2 V soaked, on its own 3.3 V regulator)\n      out = noise(2.45 - 1.25 * (wet.value / 100));\n      io.drive('AOUT', Math.min(vcc, out), 1);\n      io.draw(0.005);\n    },\n    status: () => [vcc < 3 ? 'no power' : `${Math.round(wet.value)} % wet: AOUT ${out.toFixed(2)} V`],\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('water', (part) => {\n  const depth = part.control('depth');\n  let out = 0, vcc = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      vcc = io.supply('+', '-');\n      if (vcc < 3) { io.release('S'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      const d = clamp(depth.value / 4, 0, 1);\n      out = noise(vcc * 0.82 * Math.sqrt(d)); // (rises fast once wet, then levels off)\n      io.drive('S', out, 1);\n      io.draw(0.02 * d + 0.001);\n    },\n    status: () => [vcc < 3 ? 'no power' : depth.value > 0 ? `${depth.value.toFixed(1)} cm of water: S ${out.toFixed(2)} V` : 'dry: S 0 V'],\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('mq2', (part) => {\n  const ppm = part.control('ppm');\n  const threshold = Number(part.params.threshold) || 1000;\n  let warm = 0, ao = 0, vcc = 0, tripped = false;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      vcc = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      const dt = 1 / 240;\n      if (vcc < 4) { warm = Math.max(0, warm - dt / 20); io.release('AO'); io.release('DO'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      warm = Math.min(1, warm + dt / 20); // (about 20 s to warm up)\n      // its resistance falls with gas (log-like): ~0.4 V in clean air, ~3.5 V at 10 000 ppm; cold, it\n      // reads high and drifts down while it warms\n      const g = ppm.value > 0 ? Math.log10(Math.max(1, ppm.value / 100)) / 2 : 0;\n      const settled = 0.4 + 3.1 * clamp(g, 0, 1);\n      ao = noise(vcc / 5 * (settled * warm + 2.8 * (1 - warm)));\n      io.drive('AO', ao, 1);\n      const sensed = warm > 0.9 ? ppm.value : 0;\n      tripped = sensed >= threshold;\n      io.drive('DO', tripped ? 0 : vcc, 1);\n      io.draw(0.15);\n    },\n    status: () => [vcc < 4 ? 'no power (needs 5 V for its heater)' : warm < 1 ? `warming up (${Math.round(warm * 100)} %): readings not right yet` : `${Math.round(ppm.value)} ppm: AO ${ao.toFixed(2)} V, DO ${tripped ? 'LOW (gas!)' : 'HIGH'}`],\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('flame', (part) => {\n  const flame = part.control('flame');\n  let ao = 0, vcc = 0, seen = false;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      vcc = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      if (vcc < 3) { io.release('AO'); io.release('DO'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      const f = clamp(flame.value / 100, 0, 1);\n      ao = noise(vcc * (0.95 - 0.85 * f)); // (more IR: the photodiode conducts, the output falls)\n      seen = f > 0.3;\n      io.drive('AO', ao, 1);\n      io.drive('DO', seen ? 0 : vcc, 1);\n      io.draw(0.004 + (seen ? 0.004 : 0));\n    },\n    status: () => [vcc < 3 ? 'no power' : `${seen ? 'flame seen: DO LOW' : 'no flame: DO HIGH'}, AO ${ao.toFixed(2)} V`],\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('hall', (part) => {\n  const field = part.control('field');\n  let ao = 0, vcc = 0, near = false;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      vcc = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      if (vcc < 3) { io.release('AO'); io.release('DO'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      const b = field.value; // mT\n      ao = clamp(vcc / 2 + 0.014 * (vcc / 5) * b, 0.1, vcc - 0.1);\n      // (an A3144 switches on a south pole past ~20 mT and off again under ~15: a little hysteresis)\n      near = near ? b > 15 : b > 20;\n      io.drive('AO', noise(ao), 1);\n      io.drive('DO', near ? 0 : vcc, 1);\n      io.draw(0.006);\n    },\n    status: () => [vcc < 3 ? 'no power' : `${Math.round(field.value)} mT: AO ${ao.toFixed(2)} V, DO ${near ? 'LOW (magnet)' : 'HIGH'}`],\n  };\n});\n\nbench.device('pulse', (part) => {\n  const finger = part.control('finger');\n  const bpm = part.control('bpm');\n  let phase = 0, s = 0, vcc = 0, beats = 0;\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      vcc = io.supply('+', '-');\n      if (vcc < 3) { io.release('S'); io.draw(0); return; }\n      const dt = 1 / 240;\n      if (!finger.on) {\n        s = vcc / 2 + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.02 * vcc; // (no finger: just the light in the room)\n      } else {\n        const before = phase;\n        phase = (phase + (dt * bpm.value) / 60) % 1;\n        if (phase < before) beats++;\n        // a heartbeat's light wave: a sharp rise, a small notch, a slow fall\n        const p = phase;\n        const wave = Math.exp(-(((p - 0.12) / 0.05) ** 2)) * 1.0 + Math.exp(-(((p - 0.32) / 0.07) ** 2)) * 0.35;\n        s = vcc / 2 + vcc * 0.28 * (wave - 0.25) + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.004 * vcc;\n      }\n      io.drive('S', clamp(s, 0, vcc), 1);\n      io.draw(0.004);\n    },\n    status: () => [vcc < 3 ? 'no power' : finger.on ? `finger on: ${Math.round(bpm.value)} bpm, ${beats} beats` : 'no finger: nothing to see'],\n  };\n});\n","parts":[{"id":"soil-moisture","name":"Soil moisture sensor (capacitive)","description":"A capacitive probe for plant pots: AOUT falls the wetter the soil is (about 2.4 V dry to 1.2 V soaked on 3.3-5 V). Read it with analogRead. Set how wet the soil is in the run panel.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":4,"shape":[{"box":[2.3,0.16,9.8],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[1.6,0.25,1.2],"at":[0,0.28,-4],"color":"#2a2c31","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","VCC","AOUT"],"at":[-0.254,0.16,-4.75],"dir":"x","kinds":{"GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin","AOUT":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5.5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"AOUT":{"analog":true}}}],"controls":[{"id":"wet","kind":"slider","label":"Soil wetness (%)","min":0,"max":100,"step":1,"value":35}],"device":"soil"},{"id":"water-level","name":"Water level sensor","description":"A strip of copper traces: dipped in water its S pin rises with the depth (0-4 cm), as an analog value. Set the water's depth in the run panel. (Powered all the time, the traces corrode in real life: power it from a pin and only read now and then.)","swatch":"#c0392b","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[2,0.16,6.2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#c0392b"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["S","+","-"],"at":[-0.254,0.16,-2.9],"dir":"x","kinds":{"S":"out","+":"vin","-":"gnd"},"extra":{"+":{"label":"+ (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"S":{"analog":true}}}],"controls":[{"id":"depth","kind":"slider","label":"Water depth (cm)","min":0,"max":5,"step":0.1,"value":0}],"device":"water"},{"id":"mq2","name":"Gas and smoke sensor (MQ-2)","description":"Senses smoke, LPG and methane: AO rises with the gas (analogRead), DO goes LOW past the level set by its little knob (Threshold). Its heater takes about 150 mA at 5 V and needs about 20 seconds to warm up before its readings mean anything. Set the gas in the air in the run panel.","swatch":"#2a62c8","mass":8,"params":[{"key":"threshold","label":"DO trips at (ppm)","kind":"number","min":200,"max":10000,"step":50}],"defaults":{"threshold":1000},"shape":[{"box":[3.2,0.16,2.2],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2a62c8"},{"cyl":[0.95,1.4],"at":[0.3,0.86,0],"color":"#b9bec7"},{"box":[0.5,0.5,0.5],"at":[-1.1,0.41,0.6],"color":"#2a62f0","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","DO","AO"],"at":[-1.4,0.16,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","DO":"out","AO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (5 V)","vmin":4.5,"vmax":5.5},"AO":{"analog":true}}}],"controls":[{"id":"ppm","kind":"slider","label":"Gas / smoke in the air (ppm)","min":0,"max":10000,"step":50,"value":0}],"device":"mq2"},{"id":"flame","name":"Flame sensor (IR)","description":"Sees the infrared of a flame in front of it (up to about 80 cm): AO falls the stronger the flame (analogRead), DO goes LOW past the level its knob sets. Light a flame in the run panel (how strong / how close).","swatch":"#2a62c8","mass":3,"shape":[{"box":[3,0.16,1.5],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2a62c8"},{"cyl":[0.25,0.6],"at":[1.7,0.4,0],"rot":[0,0,90],"color":"#1a1a1c"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["AO","GND","VCC","DO"],"at":[-1.4,0.16,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","DO":"out","AO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"AO":{"analog":true}}}],"controls":[{"id":"flame","kind":"slider","label":"A flame in front of it (0 none, 100 close and bright)","min":0,"max":100,"step":1,"value":0}],"device":"flame"},{"id":"hall","name":"Magnet sensor (hall effect)","description":"Feels a magnetic field: AO is half its supply with no magnet and moves up or down with a magnet's north or south pole near it (about 14 mV per mT, a 49E chip), DO goes LOW when a south pole is close (as the KY-003 / A3144). Bring a magnet near in the run panel.","swatch":"#1a1a1c","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[1.9,0.16,1.5],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"box":[0.4,0.15,0.3],"at":[0.6,0.24,0],"color":"#2a2c31","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["DO","AO","VCC","GND"],"at":[-0.85,0.16,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","DO":"out","AO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},"AO":{"analog":true}}}],"controls":[{"id":"field","kind":"slider","label":"Magnet (mT: + south pole near, - north)","min":-100,"max":100,"step":1,"value":0}],"device":"hall"},{"id":"pulse","name":"Pulse sensor (heartbeat)","description":"Shines green light into a fingertip and sees each heartbeat as a bump in the light coming back: S is an analog wave around half the supply, a peak per beat (analogRead it fast and count the peaks). Put a finger on it and set the heart rate in the run panel.","swatch":"#2e7d4f","mass":1,"shape":[{"cyl":[0.8,0.16],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2e7d4f"},{"box":[0.3,0.1,0.3],"at":[0,0.21,0],"color":"#30d158","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"S","label":"S (purple, analog)","at":[-0.5,0.16,-0.95],"kind":"out","analog":true},{"id":"+","label":"+ (3.3-5 V)","at":[0,0.16,-0.95],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"-","at":[0.5,0.16,-0.95],"kind":"gnd"}],"controls":[{"id":"finger","kind":"switch","label":"Finger on it","value":true},{"id":"bpm","kind":"slider","label":"Heart rate (beats a minute)","min":40,"max":180,"step":1,"value":72}],"device":"pulse"}],"examples":[]}